13. Any other condition that, in the investigator's judgment, might affect the study results or lead to premature termination of the study, such as alcoholism, drug abuse, other severe diseases (including mental illness) requiring concomitant treatment, severe laboratory abnormalities, or family or social factors, which could affect patient safety.

